troke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"21D2\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-21D2\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>8</sub>N<sub>2 </sub><br><br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Option (C) is correct"},"hi":{"content":"एक यौगिक में C, H और N परमाणु 9 : 1 : 3.5 के वजन अनुपात में उपस्थित हैं। यौगिक का अणु भार 108 g mol<sup>-1</sup> है। यौगिक का अणुव्यूह है","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub>N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"C<sub>3</sub>H<sub>4</sub>N"},{"identifier":"C","content":"C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>8</sub>N<sub>2</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"C<sub>9</sub>H<sub>12</sub>N<sub>3</sub>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null,"direction":null}},"permalink":"in-a-compound-c-h-and-n-atoms-are-present-in-9-1-35-y-weight-jee-main-2002-marks-4-cib7tw44tfvhbqdr.htm","updated_time":1572160200,"timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2002","topic":"quantitative-measures-in-chemical-equations","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"aieee-2002","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"4XWEvDZgov05rNf5","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","languages":["en"],"chapter":"some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry","year":2002,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2002","difficulty":"easy","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"With increase of temperature, which of these changes?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"molality"},{"identifier":"B","content":"weight fraction of solute"},{"identifier":"C","content":"molarity"},{"identifier":"D","content":"mole fraction"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Molarity = <span style=\"display: inline-block;vertical-align: middle;\">\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;border-bottom: 1px solid black;\">Number of moles of solute</div>\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;\">Volume of solution (in L)</div>\n</span>\n<br><br>Molality = <span style=\"display: inline-block;vertical-align: middle;\">\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;border-bottom: 1px solid black;\">Number of moles of solute</div>\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;\">Mass of solvent (in kg)</div>\n</span>\n<br><br>Mole fraction = <span style=\"display: inline-block;vertical-align: middle;\">\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;border-bottom: 1px solid black;\">Number of moles of component</div>\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;\">Total number of moles of all components</div>\n</span>\n<br><br>Weight fraction of solute = <span style=\"display: inline-block;vertical-align: middle;\">\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;border-bottom: 1px solid black;\">Weight of a component</div>\n     <div style=\"text-align: center;\">Total weight of solution</div>\n</span> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 100\n<br><br><b>KEY Concept :</b> Those units which are volume related will be affected by the change in temperature.\n\n<br><br>The definition of molarity is - Number of moles of solute present in one litre of solution. From definition you can see it is depends on volume which increases with increasing temperature\nand decreases with decreasing temperature.<br><br>\nAll the other three options (Molality, Mole fraction, Weight fraction of solute) are mass related units and temperature has no effect on mass."},"hi":{"content":"तापमान बढ़ने पर, इनमें से कौन सा परिवर्तित होता है?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"मोलैलिटी"},{"identifier":"B","content":"विलेय के भार अंश"},{"identifier":"C","content":"मोलरिटी"},{"identifier":"D","content":"मोल अंश"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null,"direction":null}},"permalink":"with-increase-of-temperature-which-of-these-changes-jee-main-2002-marks-4-4xwevdzgov05rnf5.htm","updated_time":1572166537,"timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2002","topic":"concentration-terms","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"aieee-2002","active":true}],"ids":["jLY8ENtJBMUyc3cU","uJ7wL8tXgwpjQUwj","cIb7tW44TFvHbqdR","4XWEvDZgov05rNf5"],"title":"AIEEE 2002 | JEE Main Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app/past-years/jee/rna-is-different-from-dna-because-rna-contains-2002-marks-4-jly8entjbmuyc3cu.htm"}